{"kind": "meta", "lane": "fp8-v3-gate", "date": "2026-08-05", "gpu": "RTX 5090 Laptop (sm_120a)", "branch": "lane/fp8-v3-gate off restructure/public-split", "shape_sheet": "27B ONLY (owner correction 2026-08-05: 'why we test 1.7b? was never part of supported models. we tune the fp8 for 27b'). Zero 1.7B cells were run; both bins retain unused 1.7B shape arrays as optional args.", "questions": {"Q1": "what is s32-vs-f32 accumulate worth on this silicon, BEFORE funding an FP8 v3", "Q2": "is native e4m3's 1.0 B/weight decode stream (vs Q8_0's 1.0625) realized as m=1 GEMV time"}, "protocol": "every A/B interleaved inside one rep loop (both arms share one clock/thermal regime); medians; flock /tmp/gpu5090.lock held per batch; temps + SM clocks recorded at hold entry/exit in the raw logs", "raw_logs": ["q1-accprobe-27b.log", "q1-accprobe-27b-confirm.log", "q1-dist-control.log", "q2-gemv-e4m3-27b.log", "q1-sass-census.txt"]}
{"kind": "instrument", "q": "Q1", "file": "crates/memra-engine/cu/mmq_q8_0_f32acc.cu", "what": "the Q8_0 MMQ FLOOR kernel with the accumulator as its ONE free variable, both arms in one TU (templated on bool F32ACC) sharing every loader, smem expression and launch parameter", "arm_s32": "mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k32.row.col.s32.s8.s8.s32 (the floor's own MMA)", "arm_f32": "mma.sync.aligned.kind::f8f6f4.m16n8k32.row.col.f32.e4m3.e4m3.f32 (the op v2 accumulates in)", "why_legal": "identical fragment ABI at this shape (4x b32 A, 2x b32 B, 4-reg D), so the swap is one instruction and nothing else", "why_not_measured_on_v2s_kernel": "v2 chains four k32 MMAs into one accumulator and folds ONCE per 128-k scale block where the floor folds every k32 \u2014 v2's epilogue f32 work is already strictly CHEAPER than the floor's, so the fold count cannot be the residual gap. Swapping inside the floor holds tiles/traffic/occupancy/fold-count fixed.", "bound_direction": "delta is an UPPER BOUND on a v3: a real v3 would additionally pay per-128-block e4m3 mantissa extraction, which this instrument does not charge", "not_a_numeric_claim": "the two arms compute different arithmetic on the same bytes by construction; this measures TIME only. Exactness is owned by fp8-mmq-check / kernel-check.", "bench": "crates/memra-engine/src/bin/accprobe_bench.rs (GEMM-only; activation pre-quantized host-side so no quantizer sits in the timed region, and magnitudes clamped <=126 so no byte is the e4m3 NaN code 0x7F)"}
{"kind": "instrument_validation", "q": "Q1", "tool": "cuobjdump --dump-sass + --dump-resource-usage", "mma_count": {"all_four_instantiations": 128}, "mma_class": {"s32_arms": "IMMA.16832.S8.S8", "f32_arms": "QMMA.16832.F32.E4M3.E4M3"}, "total_instr": {"f32_needcheck_false": 2680, "f32_needcheck_true": 2824, "s32_needcheck_false": 3176, "s32_needcheck_true": 3312}, "i2fp_converts": {"f32_arms": 0, "s32_arms": 512}, "lds": {"all": 232}, "ldg": {"all": 104}, "resources": {"all_four": "REG:255 SHARED:1024 LOCAL:0 CONSTANT[0]:944", "stack": {"f32_needcheck_false": 8, "f32_needcheck_true": 56, "s32_arms": 0}}, "read": "identical MMA count, identical REG/SHARED (so not an occupancy artifact). The S32 arm executes MORE instructions (3176 vs 2680) and pays 512 extra int->float converts, and still wins ~20% => the delta is MMA throughput of the accumulator class, not instruction count or traffic. The instrument is generous to F32.", "log": "q1-sass-census.txt"}
